{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgANqtJsCVsm8x789JRDo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `Hijack()` in `response_writer.go`. It used to fail whenever anything had been written, including just the headers. Now it only fails once body bytes have been written (`w.size > 0`). This matters because websocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket` send the headers before they hijack the connection, and the old check broke them.\n\n- I changed the error text to `\"gin: response body already written\"` to match.\n- I added a test case where hijacking right after `WriteHeaderNow()` succeeds. The existing case where hijacking after a body write fails still passes.\n- `go test ./...` passes and `gofmt` reports nothing.\n\nThe changes are not committed. The commit failed because git has no author name or email set up here, and I didn't want to set that for you. Run `git config user.name/user.email` and I'll commit, or commit it yourself.\n\nBehaviour change: a handler that sends headers and then hijacks now gets the connection instead of an error. That's the point of the fix, but any caller that relied on the error will see the difference."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":379,"cache_read_input_tokens":35045,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":379,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"16bc5a15-42c0-479e-a407-d63e981299d6","uuid":"772b04d3-e18e-483d-b855-bc999914a72b","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:01:45.999Z","request_id":"req_011CgANqt6hsweNysuTRv6zg"}
